{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_pair_channel_branch_b","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_pair_channel_branch_b","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_growth_trichotomy"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linearGrowthExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linearGrowthExponent","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L141-L180","doc":"A `GrowthExponent` with linearly growing sequence and `β = 1`.  `beta_upper` and `beta_lower` are the two halves of the\nlimsup; both reduce to the rpow-growth lemmas after splitting\n`κ^(1±ε) = κ · κ^(±ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.eventually_lt_rpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.eventually_lt_rpow","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**Eventually** `c < κ^e`, in the \"for all large κ\" form `beta_upper`\nneeds — `exists_large_rpow` gives one index, monotonicity of `x ↦ x^e`\nin the base extends it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_forces_beta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_forces_beta_one","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L122-L123","doc":"**Alias** of `QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_seq_forces_beta_one`.\n\n---\n\n**A linearly growing sequence has exponent `1`.**\n\nThe dual of `bounded_seq_forces_beta_zero`.  If `a_κ ≥ A·κ` eventually\nwith `A > 0`, then no exponent below `1` can be an upper exponent:\n`beta_upper` at `ε = (1 - β)/2` would give `A·κ ≤ κ^s` with\n`s = (1+β)/2 < 1`, i.e. `A·κ^(1-s) ≤ 1` — but `κ^(1-s)` is unbounded.\nNo fit and no precision claim enters.  (Its former reading as \"branch B\nfor the pair channel\" is withdrawn; file docstring.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_seq_forces_beta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_seq_forces_beta_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L67-L120","doc":"**A linearly growing sequence has exponent `1`.**\n\nThe dual of `bounded_seq_forces_beta_zero`.  If `a_κ ≥ A·κ` eventually\nwith `A > 0`, then no exponent below `1` can be an upper exponent:\n`beta_upper` at `ε = (1 - β)/2` would give `A·κ ≤ κ^s` with\n`s = (1+β)/2 < 1`, i.e. `A·κ^(1-s) ≤ 1` — but `κ^(1-s)` is unbounded.\nNo fit and no precision claim enters.  (Its former reading as \"branch B\nfor the pair channel\" is withdrawn; file docstring.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.exists_large_rpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.exists_large_rpow","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L53-L65","doc":"**Every positive level is eventually exceeded by `n^e`, `e > 0`** — the\none archimedean fact all three growth arguments below need, factored out\nso each of them is bookkeeping.  Returns an index that is also `≥ M`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}